<title>USA: Sony's Columbia Pictures signs deal with Spike Lee.</title>
<headline>Sony's Columbia Pictures signs deal with Spike Lee.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp's Columbia Pictures unit Friday said it signed a long-term, first-look deal with director and producer Spike Lee.</p>
<p>Under terms of the contract, Lee will write, direct and produce a number of films for the studio and maintain an office on Columbia's Culver City lot in addition to his New York offices.</p>
<p>Lee received an Academy Award nomination for his film &quot;Do the Right Thing&quot;. He is also the writer and director of &quot;Clockers&quot;, &quot;Crooklyn&quot; and &quot;Malcom X&quot;.</p>
</text>
